## Why This Is Asked
Gauge ability to design end-to-end CAPA around privilege management, multi-tenant risk, and cross-region controls.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Policy-as-code and RBAC for service accounts
- Canary rollout and RCA templates
- Observability across tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch (Node.js/Express)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // create CAPA with linked logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa_001' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle false positives and ensure minimal tenant impact?
- What data retention/privacy considerations apply to CAPA artifacts and logs?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region
